## Current Session (2026-09-06) — 🔴 committed secret found; branch + plugin cleanup

**🔴 BLOCKER — live API key committed to a PUBLIC repo.**
`zsh/.zshrc` exports a hardcoded `DC_API_KEY`. It is present in **HEAD**, not just
history — on `origin/main`, `origin/dev`, and `origin/feature/email-dispatcher-restructure`.
First committed 2025-12-17 (`3262c691b`); ~9 months of public exposure on
github.com/Data-Wise/flow-cli. Every other secret in that file already loads from
Keychain; this one line is the exception.

Fix, in this order:
1. **Rotate the key at the provider.** Only this revokes the exposure — no git
   operation undoes it. Assume scraped.
2. Store it: `security add-generic-password -a "$USER" -s dc_api_key -U -w '<new key>'`
3. Commit the fix already sitting uncommitted in the working tree — it swaps the
   literal for `security find-generic-password -a "$USER" -s dc_api_key -w`.
4. History rewrite is optional and secondary; it does not un-expose anything.

**Also found:** `zsh/functions/obs.zsh` is a dangling symlink to
`/Users/dt/projects/dev-tools/obsidian-cli-ops/src/obs.zsh` — the pre-migration
username. Untracked; `rm` it (`obs` was removed from flow-cli in v7.14).

**Done this session (flow-cli):** deleted all 10 stale local branches after
verifying each has a merged PR whose merge commit is an ancestor of `dev`
(`gh-pages` deliberately kept). Local branches now: `dev`, `gh-pages`, `main`.

**Done this session (outside flow-cli):** reconciled Claude plugin config against
the pre-migration Mac — `Data-Wise/dotfiles` PRs #23 and #24 merged; 34 → 28
enabled plugins, 18,408 → 11,613 always-on tokens (−37%). See memory
`claude-plugin-scoping-and-token-cost`.

