## Previous Session (2026-09-04) — v7.17.2 SHIPPED: CI hardening + PATH fix ✅

**Session activity:**
- **Tap release workflow unblocked** (PR #499): `Data-Wise/homebrew-tap` enabled branch
  protection on `main`, so the release workflow's direct push started failing with GH006
  (first seen on atlas v0.14.0, 2026-07-19). The tap step now commits to a per-version
  `bot/flow-cli-<version>` branch, opens a PR idempotently via `gh`, and enables squash
  auto-merge with an immediate-merge fallback. Fixed ecosystem-wide in the same pass
  (atlas#101, homebrew-tap#168, craft, folio, scribe).
- **Tap App token scoped down** (PR #514): `homebrew-release.yml` minted its credential with
  no `permission-*` inputs, so the token inherited every permission the App installation held
  on the tap — for a whole job running `sed`, `git` and `gh` against it. Now declares the two
  it actually uses: `contents: write` (formula push) + `pull-requests: write` (open/auto-merge
  the bump PR). Both confirmed already-granted from the App's 7 authored tap PRs.
- **Dependabot pinned to `dev`, npm ecosystem dropped** (PR #515): without `target-branch`,
  dependabot re-derives its base from the repo default (`main`) and **resets it on every
  rebase** — confirmed live on #503, so a manual per-PR retarget can never stick. npm updates
  dropped outright: `package.json` has no runtime dependencies, only 3 devDependencies that
  never reach a user (flow-cli ships as zsh via Homebrew); 9 of the last 16 npm dependabot PRs
  were closed unmerged, each costing a full CI run.
- **`~/.local/bin` added to `PATH`** (PR #513): `uv` installs tool shims there (`radian`,
  `arxiv_latex_cleaner`) but nothing put the directory on `PATH` — installed yet unreachable,
  surfaced while restoring a new Mac. One guarded line in `zsh/.zshenv` (not `.zshrc`, so
  non-interactive shells and Claude Code resolve them too), substring-guarded so nested shells
  don't grow `PATH` unboundedly.
- Dependency bumps: prettier 3.9.4 → 3.9.6, lint-staged 17.0.8 → 17.4.1 (devDependencies only).
- Post-release: `91ef2c0f` pointed the RELEASES.md v7.3.0–v7.17.2 gap at `CHANGELOG.md`
  rather than backfilling it. Still unreleased on `dev`.

## Previous Session (2026-08-23) — v7.17.1 SHIPPED: alias-proof shipped pipelines ✅

**Session activity:**
- **A user alias on a coreutil could hijack every shipped pipeline** (PR #509). Dispatchers run
  in the user's *interactive* shell, where aliases are live and expand at parse time. This
  machine has `tr='track-activity report'`, so every `... | tr -d ' '` in `lib/` ran that
  command and *its* output landed in the variable where a count belonged — `teach deploy
  --dry-run` printed `Would deploy Monthly Terminal Report (2026-08):` where `675` belonged.
- Root cause found by tracing the garbled uncommitted-file count shipped in v7.17.0; the
  **pre-existing** `file_count` line had the identical bug. One root cause, two symptoms — the
  new feature just made it visible.
- Fix: 101 pipeline sites across 34 files switched to `command tr`, which bypasses aliases and
  functions. Guarded by `tests/test-alias-shadowing.zsh`, including a **negative control** so
  the test cannot pass vacuously if the environment stops reproducing the hijack.

## Previous Session (2026-08-23) — v7.17.0 SHIPPED: teach deploy safety + CI coverage ✅

**Session activity:**
- **`teach deploy --dry-run` was neither read-only nor usable in CI mode** (PR #505). `ci_mode`
  auto-detects whenever stdin is not a TTY, so *every* automation or agent caller gets it, and
  two preflight gates aborted before the plan could render ("production has new commits",
  "uncommitted changes") — neither of which can affect a run that mutates nothing. The
  uncommitted-changes handler had a worse edge: interactively it **prompts to commit**, and a
  pty wrapper (`script -q /dev/null …`) answers the default `Y` and silently created a real
  commit against a live course repo, observed once. Both gates now skip when `dry_run` is true;
  real deploys still abort on both. `tests/test-teach-deploy-dryrun-readonly.zsh` — 10
  assertions, each checking repository state before *and* after.
- **`teach deploy --direct` now merges with `--no-ff`** (same PR): without it, a deploy of N
  draft commits fast-forwards production to draft's tip, leaving no single commit representing
  the deploy — so `--rollback`, which reverts the deploy commit, could only undo the last of the
  N. `git-helpers.zsh` already assumed `--no-ff` topology when filtering production conflicts.
  Guarded by `tests/test-teach-deploy-merge-topology.zsh`. **Non-obvious:** draft and production
  legitimately point at the same commit *after* a deploy (the deploy syncs draft from
  production), so ref equality is not evidence of a fast-forward — parent count is.
- **`teach deploy --dry-run` now names what it is NOT showing** — a dry run skips the
  uncommitted-changes handler, so its file list is committed work only, while a real deploy
  would offer to commit dirty files and ship them too. It now reports the excluded count.
- **Four CI coverage gaps closed** (PR #506), from a read-only audit:
  1. The two suites added in #505 merged green while CI never executed their 12 assertions —
     `run-all.sh` takes an explicit `run_test` list, not a glob. Both wired.
  2. Audited all 118 `test-*.zsh` files unreferenced by `run-all.sh`: 74 passed on a runner and
     had simply never run; 37 genuinely broken.
  3. + 4. Changelog parity and docs gating.
  Framing from the same audit: the blocking full-suite gate is real coverage, not theater — the
  `rc 77` clean-skip protocol is barely used.
- Also shipped in v7.17.0: `em undo` (single-step, 1-hour window, on `lib/em-cache.zsh`'s
  existing API), `em move --recent <ID>...` (quick-pick from the last 3 destinations, no `fzf`),
  and a centralized `ALIASES` section in `em help` — the Phase 3 work specced in
  `docs/specs/SPEC-em-ux-refactor-2026-07-07.md`.

